{
  "description": "Positive control for DIV-2. Every sensitivity tier must be representable while carrying PII, including SECRET, so this fixture must produce no violations at all.\n\nAn earlier version of this package rejected SECRET+PII as PII_AUTO_PROMOTED_TO_SECRET unless the object carried a secret_justification field — a field every V1 schema forbids via additionalProperties:false. That made a schema-valid object permanently invalid with no way to satisfy the rule. It was also wrong on its own terms: co-occurrence is not causation, and an object may be SECRET for a reason unrelated to the personal data it happens to contain.\n\nThis fixture checks orthogonality and nothing else. The separate rule that a SECRET object may not enter a ContextPack is unchanged and is covered by g_secret_in_context_pack.",
